Added a `nautobot-cable-data-model` checker (Nautobot 3.2+) flagging App and Job code affected by the Cable data model changes. Rules cover references the backwards-compatibility shims cannot rewrite, which fail outright — in ORM queries and in `Model._meta.get_field()`, which now raises `FieldDoesNotExist` for fields that survive only as properties — (`nb-removed-cable-field`, `nb-removed-termination-a-b-field`, `nb-removed-cable-path-field`, `nb-removed-cable-peer-field`); lookups the shims rewrite while raising a `DeprecationWarning` (`nb-deprecated-cable-lookup`, `nb-deprecated-termination-a-b-lookup`); assignment to a termination's now read-only `cable` attribute (`nb-readonly-cable-attribute`); and single `exclude()` calls spanning both cable ends, which the shim applies per end rather than as a combined negation (`nb-termination-a-b-exclude-both-ends`).
